{% comment %}
  AP Networking Grade Reporter wiring v2
  Include in theme.liquid just before </body>: {% render 'apcs-networking-reporter' %}

  Loads assets/ap-networking-reporter.js on the AP Networking pages that carry a
  gradeable widget. The hubs (ap-networking, ap-networking-unit-N), the ten study
  games and the topic overview pages carry none, so the script never loads there.
  The reporter also self-gates: with no [data-course="ap-networking"] wrapper, or
  no apcse_token, it does nothing, so anonymous SEO traffic is unaffected.

  Grades post to POST /api/progress/attempt (the manifest-gated path, same as
  ap-csa). Visits are already tracked by the sitewide track block, so this file
  is grades only.

  WHY THE LAB PREFIX IS HERE, ADDED 2026-08-26
    v1 matched 'ap-networking-lesson-' only. That is the handle shape of the 22
    topic lesson pages, and it was written when they were the only pages that
    reported. The four browser labs shipped later under a different shape,
    ap-networking-lab-{N}-{slug}, and nothing connected the two facts. So the
    labs rendered, scored themselves on screen, told the student "Recorded: 6 out
    of 8", and posted nothing: the function they call to report,
    window.APNET_reportAttempt, is defined by the asset this snippet loads, and
    on those four handles the asset was never on the page. Every one of the 32
    lab points was a denominator no student could earn, and the only symptom was
    a gradebook column of zeros that looked like students skipping the work.

    The labs were correct on every other side of the contract. Each page carries
    <div data-course="ap-networking" data-lesson-id="lab-N" data-item-id="lab-N">,
    each computes score and a {q, sel, ok} detail array, and NET_LABS in the
    progress API seeds lab-1 through lab-4 at 8 points, matching the 8
    checkpoints each lab renders. One missing prefix was the whole defect.

  WHAT THE PREFIX ALSO MATCHES, AND WHY THAT IS FINE
    Eight handles begin ap-networking-lab-. Four are the browser labs above. The
    other four (ap-networking-lab-1-4, -2-2, -3-5, -4-3) are the interactive
    terminal labs, which render through /lab-player.js and post to
    /api/progress/attempt themselves. Those pages carry no
    [data-course="ap-networking"] wrapper and dispatch no 'apnet:attempt', so the
    reporter's own gate makes it inert there: getContext() returns null and
    postAttempt returns before it builds a body. There is no path to a double
    post. Narrowing the match to exclude them would trade a proven no-op for a
    pattern that breaks the next time a lab is numbered differently.

  THE INVARIANT, NOT THE LIST
    smoke/networking-lab-reporter.js in the progress API repo pins this. Its
    offline half checks that this gate matches every lab handle the manifest
    expects to hear from. Its live half is the one that matters: it walks the
    AP Networking pages in the sitemap and fails if ANY page that calls
    APNET_reportAttempt or dispatches apnet:attempt does not also load this
    asset. That check knows nothing about handle conventions, so it catches the
    next page family that ships under a shape nobody thought to add here.
{% endcomment %}
{%- if page.handle contains 'ap-networking-lesson-' or page.handle contains 'ap-networking-lab-' -%}
<script src="{{ 'ap-networking-reporter.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}
